From 76cbe6f7dfa40577f8fe5f681ad1dfc6cd311b72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:08:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Verify source signatures with openpgpverify

Replace the direct GnuPG verification with %openpgpverify, which
uses Sequoia sqv, as part of the Fedora 45 Change
https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Sequoia_openpgpverify

Refresh samba-pubkey_AA99442FB680B620.gpg from keyservers/WKD: same
certificate(s), with self-signatures our copy was missing; the commands
are in the spec comment.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 samba-pubkey_AA99442FB680B620.gpg | Bin 2290 -> 7105 bytes
 samba.spec                        |   7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

